## Summary
Running the OpenCode software in the Windows user directory resulted in severe issues, such as consuming 100GB of storage space and potentially crashing the system. This incident highlights problems with software quality and the risks of inadequate performance.

## Key Points
- OpenCode exhibited poor performance when executed in the Windows user directory.
- It allocated an excessive 100GB of space, leading to storage issues.
- The problem could escalate to system instability or crashes.
- This underscores the critical need for robust software quality control.


